    timings: "Not officially specified; access may be limited or restricted depending on local arrangements. About This Site Masjid Hudaybiyah is a respected and historically significant mosque located in the area of al-Hudaybiyah, near Makkah. It marks the general location associated with one of the most important events in Islamic history: the \"Treaty of Hudaybiyyah\", signed in 6 AH between the Muslims of Madinah and the Quraysh of Makkah. The mosque stands as a reminder of the patience, wisdom, and long-term vision shown by the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and his noble companions during a challenging moment in their journey. It was here that the Muslims, though prevented from entering Makkah, remained calm, trusted the guidance of the Prophet ﷺand accepted a treaty that would later bring great blessings to the Muslim community. Masjid Hudaybiyah is also connected with the well-known miracle of the \"Well of Hudaybiyah\", where water flowed abundantly after the Prophet ﷺ poured the remaining water from his rinsing into the well. This beautiful event is remembered as a sign of Allah’s support for His Messenger ﷺ and his devoted followers.",
